{
  "about": "AC-3 hostile corpus for RUNNING a propose_actions card (action_run::check_card). The B-rule corpus (hostile_corpus_actions_2026-10-31.json) covers what a model may PROPOSE; these rows cover what the app may RUN when Apply is pressed, in the states a card can meet: Session mode on, a generation running, a finalized world, a card edited into a shape the validator would not make (a dictionary crosses the Godot boundary), an action with no click path. Each row: `items` (id, route, gated, each optional so a missing field is a row) and `ctx` (session, generating, finalized), `expect` the exact ordered list of [id-or-null, rule] refusals ([] means Apply may run). It only grows: never edit or delete a row, add rows.",
